      "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 435 opened 2023 with gross claims outstanding of GBP 1,331.3m. Analysis of the gross claims development triangle shows net favourable prior-year development of GBP 46.4m (a ~3.5% release of opening reserves) driven by mixed movements across older underwriting years (2014-2021): several years produced releases while some years (notably middecade cohorts) showed modest adverse movements. Underlying drivers called out in the report include favourable claims development in parts of the portfolio, social and economic inflation and litigation trends (ASHE and impending Ogden/discount rate changes), and geopolitical litigation impacts related to Russia/Ukraine which affected Aviation. The overall prior year movement is therefore a net release but the portfolio contains both releases and strengthenings by line.",
